                        CINCPAC for Polad, New Delhi, London, Vientiane, Bangkok, Singapore, Phnom
                    Penh, Ottawa, Paris, and Geneva.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d91-f2" n="2" xml:id="d91-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="#d55">Document 55</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d91-f3" n="3" xml:id="d91-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d90-f2">footnote 3, Document 90</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d91-f4" n="4" xml:id="d91-f4-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d91-f5" n="5" xml:id="d91-f5-content">
                <p>Neither found.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d91-f6" n="6" xml:id="d91-f6-content">
                <p>In telegram 2340 from New Delhi, March 9, Ambassador Galbraith agreed with the argument presented in this telegram
                    that a proposed note to the ICC would be unwise.
                    (Department of State, Central Files, 751G.00/3-962)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
